# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Bearing 17 Waits for the Break

**Story & Context:** At 130 BPM, Freja begins with Lur A holding a low stable ANCHOR while Lur B slowly increases PRESSURE toward a higher partial. Tiago keeps the batida pattern deliberately narrow: compact kick, one dry clap, and two tom events per bar. Hats disappear as the unstable overtone begins to wobble. The instant Lur B hits BREAK, Jonas places one woodblock strike but the bass remains silent. Only after SETTLE does Tiago authorize a short fifth-degree bass pulse and Marta answers with one prepared-clavinet open fifth. Midway through, the roles reverse so Lur B holds while Lur A drifts. Nuno enters with one breath-heavy baritone-sax pedal during the second SETTLE. The hook is the delay between audible pitch jump and harmonic confirmation.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Harbor bearing chart marked 17, two bronze curves representing the lurs, one stable horizontal line and one rising pressure line that suddenly steps upward, foghorn repair tags on a steel bench. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “bearing seventeen,” “hold the partial,” “break first,” and “settle now.”

## Track 2: Valve Room Gives Back One Breath

**Story & Context:** At 134 BPM, the arrangement is built around Breath Credit. Freja plays short ANCHOR-to-BREAK phrases separated by clearly audible inhalations. Tiago allows the percussion grid to grow only immediately after each full breath: kick, clap, tom cell, then a short burst of dry hats. As the breath runs down, layers disappear one by one until only kick and lur remain. Marta uses brittle clavinet sus2 shells after every second SETTLE. Jonas replaces selected programmed claps with frame-drum rim slaps. Nuno answers the final note of each breath cycle with a short falling fourth. In the center section, Freja deliberately delays the inhale, forcing the machine groove to remain skeletal longer than expected.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Old compressed-air valve room with one pressure gauge returning slowly toward zero, a handwritten breath-count ledger, bronze horn bell reflected in black valve paint. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “one breath back,” “valve room,” “do not fill yet,” and “credit restored.”

## Track 3: The Bell Turns Before the Bass Knows

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 124 BPM and foregrounds Bell Vector. Freja holds the same partial while gradually turning Lur A from forward-facing to side-facing, reducing brightness without changing pitch. Tiago does not automate any filter; instead, the drums thin so the acoustic directional change can be heard directly. Lur B then enters on a neighboring partial, creating the closest Twin Drift interval on the EP. Marta remains silent until both horns stabilize. Jonas uses only fingertip frame-drum taps during PRESSURE. In the last minute, Freja turns both bells toward the workshop wall, producing a short natural reflection while Tiago removes bass entirely. One final BREAK occurs in reflected position, but the expected SETTLE confirmation never arrives. The EP ends with brass decay, breath, and room reflection.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Fog-signal workshop floor plan with two horn-bell arrows rotating away from a listening point, bass line shown as a blank delayed entry, cold harbor light entering through tall doors. Sparse vocal fragments limited to “turn the bell,” “bass does not know,” “face the wall,” and “leave it unsettled.”

